      ],
      "content": "SP 80 SE                          GREAT MISSENDEN         POTTER ROW 1/96                                                      (west side) Hammonds Hall Farmhouse II Probably early C17, timber-framed, cased in brick and some flint in C18 or C19. Tile hanging to upper part of front elevation.  Old tile roof, half hipped at south end; large central brick stack.  Two storeys, door opposite stack, modern casement each side, 3 first floor casements.  Later brick section added at north end, with hipped roof.  Small rear wing of early date. Interior: original timbers exposed, curved windbraces in roof.  Large stack with inglenook exposed in south room.  RCHM I p175 MON.24 Listing NGR: SP8974403118"
    }
